    "rationale": "The test depends on the internal layout of the JSON objects (`verifier`, `judge_eval`, etc.) and on the private helper `_write_jsonl`. A refactor that renames a field or changes the file format will break the test even though the behaviour under test is unchanged.",
    "suggestions": [
      "Use a higher‑level factory (`make_row(... )`, `make_attempt(... )`) that isolates the test from concrete key names.",
      "Prefer calling the public API (`compute_b_metrics`) with in‑memory objects (if the function accepts file‑like objects) to avoid coupling to file‑system details."
