    "rationale": "The test is tightly coupled to the exact shape of the internal JSONL format (verifier.raw_response, the exact wording of \"signed overflow assumed wrap\"). Any refactor of compute_b_metrics (e.g., renaming a field or changing the JSON layout) will break the test even though the external contract may be unchanged.",
    "suggestions": [
      "Replace the literal dictionaries with builder functions or data‑class instances that hide implementation details.",
      "Assert only on the behavioural contract (e.g., “logic_error present”) rather than on the exact raw JSON string.",
